+// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+// PatternFlow - the exhibit: one panel, anonymous visitors, no menus
+//
+// A panel on a plinth. Whoever walks up gets four knobs and nothing that can
+// break the evening:
+//
+//   K4        switches between the exhibit's patterns - and only those
+//             (exhibit_presets.h) - every PF_EXHIBIT_DETENTS_PER_STEP detents,
+//             at once, wrapping round. The pattern never sees K4, and neither
+//             does MIDI: no CC 27, no note 63.
+//   K1-K3     one position per knob, 0..1, kept here and shared by every
+//             pattern (see "K1-K3" below): each pattern's parameter is that
+//             position in the parameter's own range, and - in a build whose
+//             midi feature has PF_MIDI_OUT_LANE_ABSOLUTE - CC 24-26 out to
+//             the DAW is the same position. What the room sees and what it
+//             hears come from one number.
+//   holds     the device's long-press screens cannot be opened (see
+//             lockMenus below). Brightness lives on the web console.
+//   idle      nobody touches anything for PF_EXHIBIT_IDLE_RETURN_MS: back to
+//             the default pattern, once, with the knob positions back at
+//             their starts and every pattern's listed variables put back
+//             where they started (PF_EXHIBIT_REST_VARS). Every boot starts on
+//             the default too.
+//   caption   "ARTIST / Title" over the pattern for a moment after a switch;
+//             on or off from /api/exhibit without a rebuild.
+//
+// Every one of those is a hook in features/pf_feature.h; no core file knows
+// this feature exists. Threading: every hook except appendStatus and the
+// /api/exhibit handlers runs on the frame task (loop()), so the state below
+// is plain; the few fields the network core reads or writes are atomics or
+// are written once in setup(). setup() runs before the network task is
+// started (PFFeatures::setup() precedes PatternflowNetTask::begin() in
+// patternflow.ino), and that task serves no route until loop() has
+// registered them all (servicesReady), so nothing on that core can read
+// those fields before setup() wrote them.
+//
+// What this feature resets, and what it does not: a preset's setup() runs
+// once, at boot, for every compiled-in pattern (patternflow.ino), and
+// switching to a preset does not run it again. So between idle returns each
+// pattern keeps its own state and its clock across K4 switches - but not its
+// K1-K3 values: those are the shared knob positions, so a pattern K4 comes
+// back to shows the knobs as they are now, not as it was left. The idle
+// return puts the positions back to their starts (PF_EXHIBIT_KNOB_START_n)
+// and the variables listed in PF_EXHIBIT_REST_VARS back to what they held on
+// the first frame, for all the patterns at once - which for the knob
+// variables themselves is overwritten by the positions on the next update,
+// and for state a button toggles is what puts it back; clocks run on.
+//
+// License: MIT
+// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
